To Whom It May Concern:

Pursuant to the Illinois Freedom of Information Act., I hereby request the following records:

1. Records sufficient to show all actions, entries, submissions, approvals, modifications, edits, updates, status changes, record creations, and deletions performed by the user account assigned to Robin Vaughn during the requested period.

2. Audit logs identifying actions performed by that user account between March 1, 2022, and July 31, 2022.

3. User activity logs, transaction logs, change-history logs, access logs, system logs, or similar records identifying the date, time, system utilized, record type, and action performed by that user account.

4. Records sufficient to show the ODA business functions, role assignments, permissions, security groups, and access rights associated with that user account during the requested period.

5. Role-history reports, role-assignment records, permission-assignment records, or equivalent records identifying:

a. all assigned roles and business functions;
b. effective dates of assignment;
c. modifications to assigned roles or permissions;
d. role removals;
e. permission removals;
f. ole transfers or reassignment to other users; and
g. the identity of the user or administrator responsible for those changes.

6. Permission-change audit logs, security audit logs, access-control audit logs, or similar records showing additions, modifications, removals, transfers, revocations, or reassignment of permissions associated with that user account during the requested period.

7. Records sufficient to show disciplinary, incident-management, enrollment, attendance, scheduling, grading, status, program-management, student-information, and related actions performed by that user account during the requested period, to the extent such actions are reflected in audit logs, transaction logs, activity records, or related system records.

8. Records sufficient to show all administrator actions affecting the user account assigned to Robin Vaughn (rsvaughn1@cps.edu) during the requested period, including:

a. role assignments;
b. role removals;
d. role transfers;
e. business function assignments;
f. business function removals;
g. permission grants;
h. permission modifications;
i. permission removals;
j. security group changes;
k. access-right changes; and
l. account configuration changes.

9. Records sufficient to identify any administrator, supervisor, reviewer, approver, authorizer, or other individual who requested, approved, reviewed, authorized, implemented, or otherwise participated in any role, permission, access-right, business-function, or account-configuration change affecting that user account during the requested period.

10. Records sufficient to identify the date and time of each change, the nature of the change, the individual requesting the change, the individual approving the change, the individual implementing the change, and any associated workflow, ticket, authorization, approval, or change-management records.

I request that responsive records be provided electronically in their native format whenever possible, including Excel, CSV, PDF, database export, audit-log format, or other native electronic formats.

If any requested audit logs, activity logs, role-history records, permission-history records, approval records, workflow records, or administrator-change records do not exist, have been deleted, are no longer retained, or are not maintained by CPS, please provide records sufficient to identify:

Whether such records were created or maintained during the requested period;
The applicable records-retention schedule;
The date of destruction, deletion, or disposition, if any;
The individual, office, or department responsible for maintaining such records; and
Any alternative records that document the requested actions, permissions, role assignments, approvals, transfers, removals, or changes.

If no responsive records exist, please provide written certification that no responsive records exist.

If any portion of this request is denied, please identify the specific statutory exemption relied upon and release all reasonably segregable non-exempt portions of responsive records.

Thank you for your assistance.

Tina Pearson

The requested documents will be made available to the general public, and this request is not being made for commercial purposes.

In the event that there are fees, I would be grateful if you would inform me of the total charges in advance of fulfilling my request. I would prefer the request filled electronically, by e-mail attachment if available or CD-ROM if not.

Thank you in advance for your anticipated cooperation in this matter. I look forward to receiving your response to this request within 5 business days, as the statute requires.

Sincerely,

Tina Pearson
